what's going on patrons this is Rob and  this week you guys cast your votes and  decided that you wanted me to discuss  what would happen if two of the most  powerful entities in the respective  universes went head-to-head as we've hit  the Living Tribunal against the spectre  and so as we do each time with these  videos we're gonna go over each  character in terms of their origin and  abilities and then decide which of these  immensely powerful beings would emerge  victorious  so the Living Tribunal was created by  Stan Lee Marie Severin and herb Trump  and first appeared in 1967 s strange  tales issue number 157 now in his first  appearance The Living Tribunal appeared  to Doctor Strange and informed him that  because he had determined that the earth  had a great potential for evil that he's  simply gonna destroy it which I guess  makes sense because it's just easier  than anything else but fortunately  Doctor Strange convinces the Living  Tribunal to spare the earth by pointing  out that the planet also has potential  for good and that a sorcerer supreme  Stephen strange could be capable of  maintaining the balance between the two  forces of Earth and this first  appearance really strikes to the heart  of the reason for the living tribunals  existence within the Marvel Universe as  an entity that has existed since the  beginning of time and exists as a judge  committed to preserving the balance of  the Marvel multiverse in the event that  a universe becomes unstable the Living  Tribunal judges the universe and enacts  an appropriate punishment which usually  means that he just destroys it The  Living Tribunal is composed of three  aspects equity vengeance and necessity  each of which is represented by one of  his three faces and all of which must be  in agreement in order for him to take  any action now moving on to the living  tribunals powers it's really difficult  to create a list that fully captures  what he's capable of and I feel like I  say this a lot when it comes to these  videos but you guys really like the  ultra powerful characters so I guess  that just kind of comes with the  territory but basically the Living  Tribunal is omniscient and nearly  omnipotent and is considered the second  most powerful being in the Marvel  Universe behind only the one above all  now the little tribunal can manipulate  reality and summon other insanely  powerful cosmic entities like the  in-betweener at will he was also able to  turn the Silver Surfer into a God by  allowing him to touch the void on the  fourth side of his head which is kind of  a weird thing to say but there are four  sides to his head but only three of them  actually have faces so the Silver Surfer  touched the other side and became a god  I hope that makes sense but the Living  Tribunal can also manipulate time being  able to bring time to a standstill  throughout the entire universe  as well as speeding time up to  accelerate the death of a son which  under normal circumstances would take  billions of years now in one of his most  impressive displays of power the Living  Tribunal was able to negate the effects  of the fully assembled Infinity Gauntlet  which is capable of altering the fabric  of reality and pretty much achieving  anything its wielder desires and later  was able to restore the Infinity  Gauntlet to power now when judging  whether the Beyonder should be allowed  to retain his omnipotence within his own  universe the Living Tribunal  contemplates taking the beyonders power  away which suggests that he's capable of  taking away power from other nyama  'putin beings now after deciding that  the Beyonder was allowed to keep his  power he sealed him in a pocket universe  that he could not interfere with other  universes the Living Tribunal is also  capable of replacing one universe with  another as we see when he considers  replacing the main Marvel Universe with  the ultimate universe which he  ultimately decided against and finally  the Living Tribunal was able to absorb  protege a being that had duplicated the  tribunals power and attempted to usurp  the role of the one above all so yeah  the Living Tribunal is a being of nearly  unimaginable power and it's going to  prove to be nearly impossible to defeat  but is the specter up to the challenge  well the specter was created by Jerry  Siegel and nirn art Bailey and made his  debut in more fun Comics number 52 in  1940 now there have been a couple of  versions of the spectres origin but  we're gonna use the most recent of them  for the purpose of this video and so the  spectre is an entity that has existed  since man walked the earth and was once  an angel named a star that sided with  Lucifer during the rebellion against God  but sought forgiveness for his betrayal  now as punishment for his part in the  rebellion he's forced to serve as the  embodiment of God's wrath now eventually  his wrath grows so great that he rejects  the very concept of mercy and from that  point on has to be bonded to human hosts  out of hope that his anger would be  somewhat tempered by their humanity now  there had been multiple hosts of the  spectre but the one that we see most  frequently is a guy by the name of Jim  Corrigan now as for his powers the  spectre is one of the most powerful  entities in the DC Universe and like the  Living Tribunal is nearly omnipotent he  also possesses near omniscience  telekinesis matter in reality  manipulation and can travel through time  the spectre was able to pick up planets  and use them as weapons and by merely  walking caused earthquakes in the  demonic realm he can travel at the speed  of light and dodged a punch thrown by  the flash that was said to be traveling  fast enough to knock a planet off of its  axis the spectre is extremely adept at  using magic and is more proficient than  dr. fate who's widely considered to be  one of the most powerful magicians in DC  Comics the spectre can also manipulate  his size to grow up to the size of an  entire universe and was able to create a  supernova in the palm of his hand even  more impressively the spectres reality  warping is so advanced that he was able  to create a nexus that forged all  realities the spectre has broken the  source wall which separates the DC  Multiverse from the source of all  existence and his battle with the  anti-monitor produced enough energy to  destroy all space and time and ended up  rebooting the entire DC Universe during  crisis on Infinite Earths with all that  in mind we can see that the spectre is  also a being of ridiculous power in his  own right so the question becomes how do  we decide who wins in a battle of two  characters who are both nearly  omnipotent well I think you guys really  love putting me in this situation of  trying to find out a way to decide which  ridiculously powerful character would  beat the other because you guys do it  all the time but in this case I actually  think this one is a pretty easy call  believe it or not as powerful as both of  these guys are I don't really see this  Spectre putting up much of a fight here  now that might sound strange but these  guys are really not operating on the  same level  well yes both the spectre and The Living  Tribunal are able to work reality and  manipulate matter and while both of  these characters are tasked with issuing  judgment from a supreme deity the scales  on which they operate are vastly  different  while the spectre judges souls as the  embodiment of God's wrath The Living  Tribunal judges entire universes and  couldn't wipe them out with merely a  thought when we look at the feeds of  these two characters it's really not up  for debate that the Living Tribunal has  displayed far more power than the  Spector ever has and so I know that  these two characters were presented as  being analogs of one another in the  Marvel vs. DC miniseries in the 90s but  I don't really think that this is an  accurate comparison it's always hard to  put into words why one character is  described as nigh on nip attend and  could defeat another character that's  described the same way but I think the  best way to put this is that if the  Living Tribunal showed up in the DC  Universe I feel like he could wipe out  the entirety of it including the spectre  if he chose to with nothing more than a  wave of his hand but would that being  said guys we're gonna bring this video  to an end I love you guys you all are  amazing keep an eye out for the poll for  next week's video and I won't catch  you all later purse  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]
 

